  "raw": {
    "https://wou.edu/hr/employment/employment-application-form-faculty-unclassified-professional-positions/": {
      "title": "Employment",
      "description": "Faculty & Unclassified Professional Positions – Human Resources Employment HR Equity, Access & Compliance Benefits & Retirement Employee & Labor Relations Payroll Forms Enter Time Portal Academics Current Students Employees Give Maps Admission: BACK Admission Apply Get Info Visit Us Admission Cost Academics Life at WOU Athletics Give Human Resources Home » Employment » Faculty & Unclassified Professional Positions Menu Employment HR Equity, Access & Compliance Benefits & Retirement Employee & Labor Relations Payroll Forms Enter Time Employment Employment Application Submissions Please carefully review the required qualifications and materials listed in the Job Announcement to ensure you are submitting all required documents. Upload all required materials within the application portal. Applications that are missing any required documents will not be considered and will not move forward in the review process. Submit only the materials listed in the Job Announcement. Online Application Do you have your application materials in digital format. Start an online application . Printable Application You may download an application (PDF) . Completed applications can be emailed to employment@wou.edu , faxed, or mailed. Attach all documents requested in job post. Request Mailed Application Please call (503) 838-8490 or email your request to employment@wou.edu . Include your name, mailing address, the title of the position for which you wish to apply for and your request to receive a copy of the application form. Any additional required materials (such as cover letters, resumes, reference lists, and transcripts) that you would like to submit may be uploaded with your online application. Submitting documents through email : employment@wou.edu Faxed : 503-838-8522 Mailed : Office of Human Resources, Western Oregon University, 345 N. Monmouth Ave., Monmouth, OR 97361 (Mailed Applications, please indicate the recruitment # and/or position for which you are applying) If you need assistance while completing the form, please call 503-838-8490 during normal business hours (Monday-Friday, 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m.) CONTACT Human Resources | Employment P: 503-838-8552 | F: 503-838-8522 | E-mail: employment@wou.edu WESTERN OREGON UNIVERSITY 345 Monmouth Ave. N. Monmouth OR 97361 503-838-8000 | 1-877-877-1593 Tools Bookstore Campus Maps Canvas Find People Portal Technical Support WOU Email Technical Support Resources A-Z Index Accessibility Academic Calendar Class Schedule Net Price Calculator Jobs at WOU News Explore WOU Partnerships Student Services Freedom of Expression Immigrant Resources Western Oregon University’s Land Acknowledgement Western Oregon University in Monmouth, OR is located within the traditional homelands of the Luckiamute Band of Kalapuya. Following the Willamette Valley Treaty of 1855 (Kalapuya etc. Treaty), Kalapuya people were forcibly removed to reservations in Western Oregon. Today, living descendants of these people are a part of the Confederated Tribes of Grand Ronde Community of Oregon and the Confederated Tribes of the Siletz Indians . Accessibility Public Records Privacy Student Consumer Information WOU prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, sex, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, marital status, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression in all programs, activities and employment practices as required by Title IX, other applicable laws, and policies. Retaliation is prohibited by WOU."
    },
