    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2025/10/PF2510-Job-Announcment.pdf": {
      "title": "Position Summary:",
      "description": " \n \nAdjunct Faculty [POOL] \n \nRecruitment #: PF2510 \nReview Date: Ongoing | As Needed \nDepartment:  Modern Languages / Humanities / CLAS \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with experience and qualifications [CBA]   \n \nAbout Western Oregon University: \nWestern Oregon University is a regional public, mid-sized university – committed to changing lives, \nstrengthening communities and transforming our world. Located in Monmouth, the heart of Oregon’s \nlush Willamette Valley, WOU is about 20 minutes from Salem,the state’s capital and about 75 \nminutes from Portland, the state’s cultural hub.  \n \nWestern is one of Oregon’s oldest public institutions of higher education and was incorporated into \nthe state system as a teacher training institution in 1882. The university offers undergraduate and \ngraduate degrees in arts and sciences, education and professional areas. It’s known for small class \nsizes, a focus on sustainability and a diverse liberal arts education in a student-centered environment. \nWestern is a Hispanic Serving institution, with over 40% of undergraduates being students of color. \n \nPosition Summary: \nThe Adjunct Faculty in Spanish is responsible for providing high-quality, learner-centered education in \nSpanish language. The preferred candidate will have experience/background in order to teach all \nlevels of Spanish language, including Spanish for Heritage Speakers and writing, as well as Spanish \nfor the Professions courses. The NTT’s faculty’s position supports the Spanish major, minor, & \ncertificates, as well as the B.S. Spanish Teaching Major.  \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred \nqualifications. \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you \nmeet the following: \n● Master’s degree in Spanish \n● 1-2 Years of Teaching Spanish language as principal instructor, at a 4- year, degree conferring \nuniversity. \n● Demonstrated cultural sensitivity and respect for diverse backgrounds and varieties of Spanish \nin teaching and communication. \n \nHow to Apply: Please upload the following required materials within the application portal.  \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please \ninclude only the materials listed below: \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - unclassified/faculty \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume/CV \n \n \n \n \n4. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned \n5. Complete and submit the Reference Check form, available here along with your application \n \nBackground/Education Check: \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are \nprocessed for positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \nBenefits:    \nWestern Oregon University offers an excellent benefits package for eligible employees which includes \n95% premium paid healthcare, a generous retirement and vacation package, and reduced tuition \nrates for employee, spouse or dependent at any of the Oregon Public Universities. \nhttp://www.wou.edu/hr/benefits/ \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, \ncolor, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran \nstatus, or any other characteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences, and know that our \ndiverse team is a strength that drives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU \nactivity or event, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. \nIf you have questions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. \nPreference will be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and \nelectronically attach the required documentation at the time of application. For information regarding \nVeterans' Preference qualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nTo stay informed about the progress of this search, we invite and encourage you to explore our \ncareer page at wou.edu/hr/employment/jobs/. Unfortunately, due to the volume, it is challenging for us \nto offer individual updates on the status of each application, and for that, we sincerely regret any \ninconvenience. We thank you for your patience and interest in employment at Western Oregon \nUniversity. \n \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2026/04/PF2604-Job-Announcment-2.pdf": {
      "title": "Position Summary:",
      "description": " \n \nAdjunct Faculty - Occupational Therapy \n \nRecruitment #: PF2604 \nReview Date:  Ongoing | As needed \nDepartment:  Occupational Therapy \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with experience and qualifications  \n \nAbout Western Oregon University: \nWestern Oregon University is a regional public, mid-sized university – committed to changing lives, \nstrengthening communities and transforming our world. Located in Monmouth, the heart of Oregon’s lush \nWillamette Valley, WOU is about 20 minutes from Salem, the state’s capital and about 75 minutes from \nPortland, the state’s cultural hub.  \n \nWestern is one of Oregon’s oldest public institutions of higher education and was incorporated into the state \nsystem as a teacher training institution in 1882. The university offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in \narts and sciences, education and professional areas. It’s known for small class sizes, a focus on sustainability \nand a diverse liberal arts education in a student-centered environment. Western is an emerging Hispanic \nServing institution, with over 40% of undergraduates being students of color. \n \nPosition Summary: \nAdjunct faculty members in the Occupational Therapy Program will be responsible for teaching high-\nquality, learner-centered courses within the Occupational Therapy Doctorate Program. Topics may \ninclude occupational therapy theories, clinical conditions, evidence-based practice, human anatomy, \nmovement analysis, or classes focused on specific clinical practice areas. Primary responsibilities \ninclude designing, delivering, and managing courses across multiple instructional modalities, while \nfostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment. Faculty are expected to demonstrate \nsubject matter expertise, employ effective teaching approaches, and maintain professional standards \nin student engagement and course management. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred qualifications. \n \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you meet the \nfollowing: \n● Bachelor’s degree : Graduation from an accredited Occupational Therapy program (ACOTE \nStandard A.2.5) \n● Current license to practice OT in Oregon (ACOTE Standard A.2.5) \n● Minimum of 1 year of documented clinical practice experience in the field of occupational therapy \n● 6-12 months of demonstrated experience teaching adult learners in an occupational therapy or \noccupational therapy assistant program. \n● Excellent communication and problem-solving skills \n● Strong organizational and documentation skills \n● Demonstrated clinical and disciplinary expertise (ACOTE standard A.2.3.) \n● Demonstrated knowledge and experience working with and supporting the success of people \nwho have diverse backgrounds, cultures, or languages \n● Eligibility for Professional license, registration or certification \n● Oregon Occupational Therapist License required upon hire \n● National Board for Certification of Occupational Therapy – initial certification required \n \n \n \n \n \nHow to Apply: Please upload the following required materials within the application portal.  \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please include \nonly the materials listed below: \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - unclassified/faculty \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume \n4. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned \n5. Complete and submit the Reference Check form, available here along with your application \n \nBackground/Education Check: \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are processed \nfor positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, \nnational origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran status, or any other \ncharacteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences, and know that our diverse team is a strength that \ndrives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU activity or \nevent, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. If you have \nquestions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. Preference \nwill be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and electronically attach the \nrequired documentation at the time of application. For information regarding Veterans' Preference \nqualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nTo stay informed about the progress of this search, we invite and encourage you to explore our career page at \nwou.edu/hr/employment/jobs/. Unfortunately, due to the volume, it is challenging for us to offer individual \nupdates on the status of each application, and for that, we sincerely regret any inconvenience. We thank you \nfor your patience and interest in employment at Western Oregon University. \n \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2026/04/PF2605-Job-Announcement.pdf": {
      "title": "Position Summary:",
      "description": " \n \nAdjunct Faculty, Organizational Leadership \n \nRecruitment #: PF2605 \nReview Date: Immediate review | Open until filled \nDepartment:  Organizational Leadership \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with experience and qualifications  \n \nAbout Western Oregon University: \nWestern Oregon University is a regional public, mid-sized university – committed to changing lives, \nstrengthening communities and transforming our world. Located in Monmouth, the heart of Oregon’s \nlush Willamette Valley, WOU is about 20 minutes from Salem, the state’s capital and about 75 \nminutes from Portland, the state’s cultural hub.  \n \nWestern is one of Oregon’s oldest public institutions of higher education and was incorporated into \nthe state system as a teacher training institution in 1882. The university offers undergraduate and \ngraduate degrees in arts and sciences, education and professional areas. It’s known for small class \nsizes, a focus on sustainability and a diverse liberal arts education in a student-centered environment. \nWestern is an emerging Hispanic Serving institution, with over 40% of undergraduates being students \nof color. \n \nPosition Summary: \nAdjunct faculty members in the Organizational Leadership (OL) department will be responsible for \nteaching high-quality, learner-centered courses within the OL Master’s Program. Primary \nresponsibilities include designing, delivering, and managing courses across multiple instructional \nmodalities, while fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment. Faculty are expected to \ndemonstrate subject matter expertise, employ effective teaching approaches, and maintain \nprofessional standards in student engagement and course management. \n \nSelected applicants must reside in the state of Oregon by the time of hire. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred \nqualifications. \n \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you \nmeet the following: \n● Master’s degree in Organizational Leadership, Industrial-Organizational Psychology, Business \nAdministration, or related field \n● 1-2 years of demonstrated experience teaching adult learners in leadership related fields \n● Strong professional communication skills \n● Collaborative team player with adaptability \n \nHow to Apply: Please upload the following required materials within the application portal.  \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please \ninclude only the materials listed below: \n \n \n \n \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - unclassified/faculty \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned \n5. Complete and submit the Reference Check form, available here along with your application \n \nBackground/Education Check: \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are \nprocessed for positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, \ncolor, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran \nstatus, or any other characteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences and know that our \ndiverse team is a strength that drives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU \nactivity or event, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. \nIf you have questions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. \nPreference will be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and \nelectronically attach the required documentation at the time of application. For information regarding \nVeterans' Preference qualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nTo stay informed about the progress of this search, we invite and encourage you to explore our \ncareer page at wou.edu/hr/employment/jobs/. Unfortunately, due to the volume, it is challenging for us \nto offer individual updates on the status of each application, and for that, we sincerely regret any \ninconvenience. We thank you for your patience and interest in employment at Western Oregon \nUniversity. \n \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2025/10/v2PF2509-Job-Announcment.pdf": {
      "title": "Position Summary:",
      "description": " \n \nAdjunct Faculty [POOL] \n \nRecruitment #: PF2509 \nReview Date: Ongoing | As Needed \nDepartment:  Politics, Policy & Administration / Social Sciences \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with experience and qualifications [CBA]   \n \nAbout Western Oregon University: \nWestern Oregon University is a regional public, mid-sized university – committed to changing lives, \nstrengthening communities and transforming our world. Located in Monmouth, the heart of Oregon’s \nlush Willamette Valley, WOU is about 20 minutes from Salem, the state’s capital and about 75 \nminutes from Portland, the state’s cultural hub.  \n \nWestern is one of Oregon’s oldest public institutions of higher education and was incorporated into \nthe state system as a teacher training institution in 1882. The university offers undergraduate and \ngraduate degrees in arts and sciences, education and professional areas. It’s known for small class \nsizes, a focus on sustainability and a diverse liberal arts education in a student-centered environment. \nWestern is an emerging Hispanic Serving institution, with over 40% of undergraduates being students \nof color. \n \nPosition Summary: \nThe Adjunct Faculty Member in the Department of Politics, Policy & Administration will be responsible \nfor providing high-quality, learner-centered education in topics in politics, policy, and administration. \nPrimary responsibilities include designing, delivering, and managing courses across multiple \ninstructional modalities, while fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment. Faculty are \nexpected to demonstrate subject matter expertise, employ effective teaching approaches, and \nmaintain professional standards in student engagement and course management. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred \nqualifications. \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you \nmeet the following: \n● Master’s degree in Public Administration, Political Science, Public Policy, Law, or related field \n● 1-2 years of Teaching experience in Political Science, Public Policy, Public Administration or \nrelated field OR combination of teaching experience and related professional experience \n● Strong verbal and written communication skills \n● Engaging, dynamic, and student-centered teaching style \n \nHow to Apply: To apply for this position, please upload the following required materials within the \napplication portal.  \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please \ninclude only the materials listed below: \n \n \n \n \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - unclassified/faculty \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned \n5. Complete and submit the Reference Check form, available here along with your application \n \nBackground/Education Check: \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are \nprocessed for positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \nBenefits:    \nWestern Oregon University offers an excellent benefits package for eligible employees which includes \n95% premium paid healthcare, a generous retirement and vacation package, and reduced tuition \nrates for employee, spouse or dependent at any of the Oregon Public Universities. \nhttp://www.wou.edu/hr/benefits/ \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, \ncolor, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran \nstatus, or any other characteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences, and know that our \ndiverse team is a strength that drives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU \nactivity or event, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. \nIf you have questions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. \nPreference will be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and \nelectronically attach the required documentation at the time of application. For information regarding \nVeterans' Preference qualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nTo stay informed about the progress of this search, we invite and encourage you to explore our \ncareer page at wou.edu/hr/employment/jobs/. Unfortunately, due to the volume, it is challenging for us \nto offer individual updates on the status of each application, and for that, we sincerely regret any \ninconvenience. We thank you for your patience and interest in employment at Western Oregon \nUniversity. \n \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2026/06/PF2607-Job-Announcement.pdf": {
      "title": "Department/ Position Summary:",
      "description": " \n \nAdjunct Faculty – Anthropology/Social Science [POOL]  \n \nRecruitment #: PF2607 \nReview Date: Review as needed | Ongoing \nDepartment:  Anthropology / Social Science \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with education and experience \n \nDepartment/ Position Summary: \nThe Adjunct Faculty Member in the Department of Anthropology will be responsible for providing \nhigh-quality, learner-centered education in topics in Anthropology. Primary responsibilities include \ndesigning, delivering, and managing courses across multiple instructional modalities, while fostering \nan inclusive and supportive learning environment. Faculty are expected to demonstrate subject \nmatter expertise, employ effective teaching approaches, and maintain professional standards in \nstudent engagement and course management. \n \nPlease Note: This is a pool position, which means applications are accepted on an ongoing basis to \nbuild a qualified candidate pool. Selected applicants may be contacted as openings become \navailable. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred \nqualifications. \n \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you \nmeet the following: \n● Master’s degree in Anthropology or related field \n● 1-2 years of teaching experience in Political Science, Public Policy, Public Administration or \nrelated field OR combination of teaching experience and related professional experience \n● Strong verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to convey complex concepts \nclearly and effectively. \n● Engaging and dynamic classroom instruction that promotes student participation, critical \nthinking, and academic success. \n● Proven ability to build positive relationships with students, fostering a supportive, inclusive, and \nrespectful learning environment. \nHow to Apply:  \nTo apply for this position, please upload the following required materials within the application portal. \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration.  \n \nPlease include only the materials listed below: \n \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - unclassified/faculty \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Reference Check form available here  \n5. Transcripts for the highest degree earned \n \n \n \n \n \nBackground/Education Check: \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are \nprocessed for positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, \ncolor, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran \nstatus, or any other characteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences and know that our \ndiverse team is a strength that drives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU \nactivity or event, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. \nIf you have questions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. \nPreference will be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and \nelectronically attach the required documentation at the time of application. For information regarding \nVeterans' Preference qualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nTo stay updated on the progress of this search, we encourage you to visit our Careers page. Due to \nthe high volume of applications we receive, we're unable to provide individual updates—but please \nknow that your interest is genuinely appreciated. We sincerely thank you for your patience and for \nconsidering a future with Western Oregon University. \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2026/06/F-SUS-2025-JOB-ANNOUNCEMENT.pdf": {
      "title": "Department/ Position Summary:",
      "description": " \n \nAdjunct Faculty - Sustainability [POOL]  \n \nRecruitment #: F-SUS \nReview Date:  Review as needed | Ongoing \nDepartment:  Sustainability \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with education and experience  \n \nDepartment/ Position Summary: \nThe Adjunct Faculty Member in the Department of Sustainability will be responsible for providing \nhigh-quality, learner-centered education in topics in Sustainability. Primary responsibilities include \ndesigning, delivering, and managing courses, while fostering an inclusive and supportive learning \nenvironment. Faculty are expected to demonstrate subject matter expertise, employ effective \nteaching approaches, and maintain professional standards in student engagement and course \nmanagement. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred \nqualifications. \n \nPlease Note: This is a pool position, which means applications are accepted on an ongoing basis to build a \nqualified candidate pool. Selected applicants may be contacted as openings become available. \n \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you meet the \nfollowing: \n● Master’s Degree or PhD in Sustainability or related field.  \n● 1-2 years of teaching experience in Political Science, Public Policy, Public Administration or related \nfield OR combination of teaching experience and related professional experience \n● Communication (verbal and written): Demonstrates clear, professional, and effective communication in \nboth verbal and written interactions, ensuring students understand expectations, instructions, and \nfeedback.  \n● Engaging and dynamic classroom teaching: Uses a variety of instructional strategies and interactive \nactivities to create an engaging learning environment that promotes student participation and critical \nthinking.  \n● Positive rapport with students: Builds respectful, supportive relationships with students and fosters a \nwelcoming classroom environment where students feel valued, comfortable, and motivated to learn. \n \nHow to Apply:  \nTo apply for this position, please upload the following required materials within the application portal. \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration.  \n \nPlease include only the materials listed below: \n \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - unclassified/faculty \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Complete and submit the Reference Check form, available here along with your application \n5. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned. Official transcripts will be required if hired. \n \nBackground/Education Check: \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are processed \nfor positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \n \n \n \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, \nnational origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran status, or any other \ncharacteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences and know that our diverse team is a strength that \ndrives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU activity or \nevent, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. If you have \nquestions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. Preference \nwill be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and electronically attach the \nrequired documentation at the time of application. For information regarding Veterans' Preference \nqualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nContact Information \nFor questions regarding the application process or to submit your application documents, please contact \nHuman Resources at employment@wou.edu \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2025/12/PF2513-Job-Announcment.pdf": {
      "title": "Position Summary:",
      "description": " \n \nAdjunct Faculty - Sociology [POOL] \n \nRecruitment #: PF2513 \nReview Date:  Ongoing | As needed \nDepartment:  Sociology / Social Science \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with experience and qualifications [CBA]   \n \nAbout Western Oregon University: \nWestern Oregon University is a regional public, mid-sized university – committed to changing lives, \nstrengthening communities and transforming our world. Located in Monmouth, the heart of Oregon’s lush \nWillamette Valley, WOU is about 20 minutes from Salem, the state’s capital and about 75 minutes from \nPortland, the state’s cultural hub.  \n \nWestern is one of Oregon’s oldest public institutions of higher education and was incorporated into the state \nsystem as a teacher training institution in 1882. The university offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in \narts and sciences, education and professional areas. It’s known for small class sizes, a focus on sustainability \nand a diverse liberal arts education in a student-centered environment. Western is a Hispanic Serving \ninstitution, with over 40% of undergraduates being students of color. \n \nPosition Summary: \nThe Adjunct Faculty Member in the Department of Sociology will be responsible for providing high-quality, \nlearner-centered education in topics in Sociology. Primary responsibilities include designing, delivering, and \nmanaging courses across multiple instructional modalities, while fostering an inclusive and supportive learning \nenvironment. Faculty are expected to demonstrate subject matter expertise, employ effective teaching \napproaches, and maintain professional standards in student engagement and course management. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred qualifications. \n \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you meet the \nfollowing: \n● Master’s degree in Sociology or related field \n● College-level teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or master’s level in Political Science, Public \nPolicy, Public Administration or related field OR combination of teaching experience and related \nprofessional experience \n● Communicate effectively through clear verbal and written messaging \n● Delivers engaging, dynamic classroom instruction \n● Establishes positive, supportive relationships with students \nHow to Apply: Please upload the following required materials within the application portal.  \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. Please \ninclude only the materials listed below: \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - unclassified/faculty \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned \n5. Complete and submit the Reference Check form, available here along with your application \n \nBackground/Education Check: \n \n \n \n \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are processed \nfor positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, color, \nnational origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran status, or any other \ncharacteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences, and know that our diverse team is a strength that \ndrives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU activity or \nevent, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. If you have \nquestions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. Preference \nwill be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and electronically attach the \nrequired documentation at the time of application. For information regarding Veterans' Preference \nqualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nTo stay informed about the status of this search, we encourage you to regularly visit our careers page at \nwou.edu/hr/employment/jobs/. Due to the high volume of applications we receive, we are unable to provide \nindividual updates regarding the status of each application. We appreciate your understanding and sincerely \napologize for any inconvenience this may cause. Thank you for your interest in employment at Western \nOregon University. \n \n "
    },
    "https://cdn.wou.edu/hr/files/2025/08/PF2508-Job-Announcement-1.pdf": {
      "title": "Position Summary:",
      "description": " \n \nAdjunct Faculty – Teacher Education Generalist \n \nRecruitment #: PF2508 \nReview Date: Open | Open until filled \nDepartment:  Teacher Education/Education & Leadership \nSalary Rate:   Commensurate with experience and qualifications WOUFT \n \nAbout Western Oregon University: \nWestern Oregon University is a regional public, mid-sized university – committed to changing lives, \nstrengthening communities and transforming our world. Located in Monmouth, the heart of Oregon’s \nlush Willamette Valley, WOU is about 20 minutes from Salem,the state’s capital and about 75 \nminutes from Portland, the state’s cultural hub.  \n \nWestern is one of Oregon’s oldest public institutions of higher education and was incorporated into \nthe state system as a teacher training institution in 1882. The university offers undergraduate and \ngraduate degrees in arts and sciences, education and professional areas. It’s known for small class \nsizes, a focus on sustainability and a diverse liberal arts education in a student-centered environment. \nWestern is an emerging Hispanic Serving institution, with over 40% of undergraduates being students \nof color. \n \nPosition Summary: \nThis position serves in the Education and Leadership (DEL) Division in the College of Education \n(COE) at Western Oregon University (WOU) as a part-time adjunct faculty member in Teacher \nEducation. \n \nThis position has the primary responsibility of teaching courses within the teacher education \ncurriculum.  \nResponsibilities: \n• Teach graduate and/or undergraduate level classes in various formats (e.g., in-person, \nonline, hybrid, synchronous, asynchronous) with possible opportunities for summer, on/off \ncampus teaching \n• Complete a required WOU online training course for effective online and hybrid \ninstructional practices.  Must be done prior to the start of teaching or simultaneously \nduring the first term of teaching. \n \nFor temporary and adjunct positions, hiring is limited to candidates residing within Oregon. Out-of-state hires \nare not permitted for these appointment types. \n \nClick here for the complete position description which includes knowledge areas and preferred \nqualifications. \n \nRequired Qualifications: Please ensure your application materials clearly demonstrate how you \nmeet the following: \n● Master’s degree in education or related field \n● Evidence of three or more years of teaching experience in K-12 or higher education \n \n \n \n \nsettings \n● Have expertise in one or more of the following areas: General Elementary \nEducation, Special Education, ESOL, Bilingual Education, Literacy Education, \nScience Education, Math Education, Social Sciences Education, Developmental \nPsychology, Early Childhood Education, Diversity and Inclusion, and Education \nTechnology \n \nHow to Apply: Please upload the following required materials within the application portal.  \nApplications missing any of the required documents will not move forward for consideration. \nPlease include only the materials listed below: \n1. WOU Employment Application form available here - classified \n2. Cover Letter that outlines your qualifications and how they align with the position \n3. Resume/CV \n4. Unofficial transcripts for your highest degree earned \n5. Complete and submit the Reference Check form, available here along with your application \n \nBackground/Education Check: \nA criminal background check will be completed as a condition of employment. Education checks are \nprocessed for positions requiring a formal degree as a minimum requirement. \n \nBenefits:    \nWestern Oregon University offers an excellent benefits package for eligible employees which includes \n95% premium paid healthcare, a generous retirement and vacation package, and reduced tuition \nrates for employee, spouse or dependent at any of the Oregon Public Universities. \nhttp://www.wou.edu/hr/benefits/ \n \nEqual Employment Opportunity: \nWestern Oregon University is an equal opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based on race, \ncolor, national origin, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, religion, veteran \nstatus, or any other characteristic protected by law. We embrace our differences, and know that our \ndiverse team is a strength that drives our success.   \n \nAccommodation Requests: \nWestern Oregon University is committed to developing a barrier-free recruitment process and work \nenvironment. If you would like to request disability-related accommodation(s) to participate in a WOU \nactivity or event, please complete the online request form at least three (3) business days in advance. \nIf you have questions, contact Desiree Noah at noahd@wou.edu. \nVeterans Preference \nApplicants are eligible to use Veterans' Preference when applying with Western Oregon University in \naccordance with ORS 408.225, 408.230 and 408.235; and OAR 105-040-0010 and 105-040-0015. \nPreference will be given only if the applicant meets the minimum criteria of the position and \n \n \n \n \nelectronically attach the required documentation at the time of application. For information regarding \nVeterans' Preference qualifications, visit http://www.oregonjobs.org/DAS/STJOBS/vetpoints.shtmlq \nTo stay informed about the progress of this search, we invite and encourage you to explore our career page at \nwou.edu/hr/employment/jobs/. Unfortunately, due to the volume, it is challenging for us to offer individual updates on the \nstatus of each application, and for that, we sincerely regret any inconvenience. We thank you for your patience and \ninterest in employment at Western Oregon University. "
    },
